# Copy to apps/web/.env.local for local work. Every one of these is set on the
# deployment through the host's environment settings, never in a committed file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED everywhere, including locally.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres. There is deliberately no fallback: a missing value used to open a
# local SQLite file, which on a serverless host means a scratch database on a
# disk that is discarded between requests, so the app appears to work and saved
# sessions quietly vanish. It now refuses to start instead.
#
# A Neon branch is free and takes about a minute. Any Postgres works.
# Neon and most hosted providers require sslmode=require.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED in production. Optional locally: `pnpm dev` with none of these set
# runs in single-user local mode, which is deliberate.
#
# A production build with authentication unconfigured refuses to serve a
# request rather than exposing every saved scoping session, including client
# asset inventories, to anyone with the URL.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Signs the session cookie. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET=""

# The canonical URL of the deployment, e.g. https://stackfit.example.com
# Vercel sets this for you; set it by hand anywhere else.
# NEXTAUTH_URL=""

# At least one provider. The callback URL to register with the provider is
# <NEXTAUTH_URL>/api/auth/callback/google (or /github).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=""
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Who may sign in, comma-separated. OAuth proves identity; this grants access.
# An empty or missing list admits NOBODY: a configuration failure reads as
# "no", never as "everyone".
# STACKFIT_ALLOWED_EMAILS="analyst@example.com,lead@example.com"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL, and the weakest way in. Email-and-password accounts, for
# demonstrating the portal to a client who cannot be handed somebody's SSO.
#
# `email:password`, separated by commas or newlines. Unset means no password
# sign-in exists and the form is not drawn. These accounts do NOT need to
# appear in STACKFIT_ALLOWED_EMAILS: whoever writes this variable is the
# person who would otherwise have written that one, so a credential is both
# the identity and the grant.
#
# The passwords are here in the clear rather than as hashes in a database.
# That is the same class of secret as an API key and the host protects it the
# same way, but anyone who can read this configuration can read them, and
# there is no rotation, lockout or second factor. Prefer OAuth for real use;
# see apps/web/src/lib/credentials.ts.
# STACKFIT_CREDENTIAL_USERS="demo@example.com:choose-something-long"
